=====Usage notes=====
* {{m|la|de|Dē}} denotes the [[go out|going out]], [[departure]], [[removal]], or [[separation|separating]] of an object from any fixed point (it occupies a middle place between {{m|la|ab||away from}} which denotes a mere external departure, and {{m|la|ex||out of}} which signifies from the interior of a thing). Hence verbs compounded with {{m|la|de|dē}} are constructed not only with {{m|la|de|dē}}, but quite as frequently with {{m|la|ab}} and {{m|la|ex}}; and, on the other hand, those compounded with {{m|la|ab}} and {{m|la|ex}} often have the {{m|la|terminus a quo}} indicated by {{m|la|de|dē}}.

